      "code": "size_t hdrLen = getHeaderLen();\nif (m_DataLen <= hdrLen || hdrLen == 0)\n    return;\n\niphdr* ipHdr = getIPv4Header();\n\nProtocolType greVer = UnknownProtocol;\nProtocolType igmpVer = UnknownProtocol;\nbool igmpQuery = false;\n\nuint8_t ipVersion = 0;\n\nuint8_t* payload = m_Data + hdrLen;\nsize_t payloadLen = m_DataLen - hdrLen;",
      "note": "First project statement on the vulnerable path that materializes the attacker-controlled GRE byte slice and its length from the raw IPv4 packet tail.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "Packet++/src/IPv4Layer.cpp",
      "function": "pcpp::IPv4Layer::parseNextLayer",
      "line": null,
      "code": "else if (greVer == GREv1)\n    m_NextLayer = new GREv1Layer(payload, payloadLen, this, m_Packet);",
      "note": "The staged patch changes this branch to `else if (greVer == GREv1 && GREv1Layer::isDataValid(payload, payloadLen))`, and `GREv1Layer::isDataValid()` requires at least `sizeof(gre1_header)` (8) bytes. The witness satisfies the old 4-byte version probe but not the fixed 8-byte constructor precondition.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
